apocalyptic scenes here in Baltimore the  aftermath of a night of violent protests  an eruption of pent-up frustration among  the city's black youth rioters  vandalized businesses looted shops  pharmacies and liquor stores as the city  descended into chaos it's not a world  peace which all gotta give us that and  y'all keep coming and taking everything  we got we all take the child got we not  pan out here it's not a look we won  outright the epicenter of the violence  is West Baltimore a predominantly black  neighborhood struggling with high  unemployment and high crime rates for  years people here have been complaining  of racial discrimination and excessive  brutality by white police officers but  the city's black mayor showed little  sympathy for the rioters this is one of  our darkest days as a city and I know  that we're much better than this we know  that the world is watching and we cannot  allow our city to devolve into chaos  because I'm a you know a small group of  criminals it was the latest flare-up  over the death of Freddie gray the  protests began after his funeral  yesterday the 25 year old black man was  arrested on April twelfth and died from  a spinal injury while in police custody  witnesses say he told police he had  asthma and couldn't breathe Gray's death  is the latest of several high-profile  cases beginning with the shooting of  Michael Brown in Ferguson last year that  have fueled racial tensions across the  nation too many hear his death is seen  as further proof that black lives don't  matter
 

